Check whether √33 can be simplified:
The factors of 33 are 1, 3, 11, 33, none of which is a square number greater than 1.
Separate into the two exact solutions:
x = \frac{−5 + \sqrt{33}}{4}
or
x = \frac{−5 − \sqrt{33}}{4}

